Step 2: Divide each side in three equal parts. This is why it is handy to have
the sides divisible by three.

Step 3: Draw an equilateral triangle on each middle part. Measure the
length of the middle third to know the length of the sides of these new
triangles

Step 4: Divide each outer side into thirds. You can see the 2nd generation of
triangles covers a bit of the first. These three line segments shouldn't be
parted in three.

Step 5: Draw an equilateral triangle on each middle part.
